<p><a name="fn20"></a> 20. The Federal Reserve's Model Risk Management guidance (SR 11-7) establishes an expectation that models used in banking are conceptually sound or "fit for purpose." SR 11-7 instructs that when evaluating a model, supervised institutions should consider the "[t]he design, theory, and logic underlying the model." The Model Risk Management guidance discusses in detail the tools banks rely on to help establish the soundness of their models, such as back-testing and benchmarking and other outcomes-based tests. <a href="#f20">Return to text</a></p>
                     
